---
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Three Walnut Frames — Heartwood Stand</title>

    <style>
      :root {
        --bg: #f5f1ea;
        --surface: #fbf8f3;
        --text: #1f1c17;
        --muted: #5e5a53;
        --accent: #6f7c68;
        --max-width: 760px;
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
      }

      body {
        font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--text);
        line-height: 1.7;
      }

      .site-header {
        padding: 1.25rem 2rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
      }

      .site-nav {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: space-between;
      }

      .site-brand a {
        color: var(--text);
        text-decoration: none;
        font-size: 1rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .site-menu {
        display: flex;
        gap: 1.25rem;
      }

      .site-menu a {
        color: var(--muted);
        text-decoration: none;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
      }

      .site-menu a:hover {
        color: var(--text);
      }

      .journal-header {
        max-width: var(--max-width);
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 4rem 1.5rem 2rem;
      }

      .journal-header h1 {
        font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
        line-height: 1.15;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
      }

      .journal-meta {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        font-style: italic;
      }

      .journal-body {
        max-width: var(--max-width);
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 2rem 1.5rem 4rem;
      }

      .journal-body p {
        margin-bottom: 1.35rem;
        font-size: 1.08rem;
      }

      .journal-image {
        margin: 2.5rem 0;
      }

      .journal-image img {
        width: 100%;
        border-radius: 3px;
        display: block;
      }

      .journal-image figcaption {
        margin-top: 0.5rem;
        font-size: 0.88rem;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-style: italic;
      }

      .image-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        gap: 12px;
        margin: 2.5rem 0;
      }

      .image-grid img {
        width: 100%;
        height: 260px;
        object-fit: cover;
        border-radius: 3px;
        display: block;
      }

      footer {
        padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 3rem;
        text-align: center;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.98rem;
        border-top: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
      }

      .back-link {
        display: inline-block;
        margin-bottom: 3rem;
        color: var(--muted);
        text-decoration: none;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.03em;
      }

      .back-link:hover {
        color: var(--text);
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <nav class="site-nav">
        <div class="site-brand">
          <a href="/">Heartwood Stand</a>
        </div>
        <div class="site-menu">
          <a href="/">Home</a>
          <a href="/journal">Journal</a>
        </div>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <div class="journal-header">
      <a href="/journal" class="back-link">← Journal</a>
      <h1>Three Walnut Frames</h1>
      <p class="journal-meta">March 2026</p>
    </div>

    <div class="journal-body">

      <figure class="journal-image">
        <img src="/images/journal/walnut-frames/Trio.webp" alt="Three walnut frames arranged together" />
      </figure>

      <p>
        A desire to find a home for three images started this project. 
        That's where this work began.
      </p>

      <p>
        A black walnut board, rough cut, had been waiting in the shop 
        for over a year. Some passes on the joiner, a few runs through 
        the planer and the grain showed itself. Looked promising.
      </p>

      <p>
        Slow experimenting at the miter saw taught how to close the miters.
      </p>

      <div class="image-grid">
        <img src="/images/journal/walnut-frames/AllCorner.webp" alt="Miter joint detail" />
        <img src="/images/journal/walnut-frames/TrioCorner.webp" alt="Corner joinery" />
      </div>

      <p>
        The glue up went smoothly. Some sanding up through 220 and then 
        a few coats of Danish oil seemed to really let the grain pop. 
        Sometimes less is more when the material is right.
      </p>

      <figure class="journal-image">
        <img src="/images/journal/walnut-frames/Grain.webp" alt="Walnut grain detail" />
      </figure>

      <div class="image-grid">
        <img src="/images/journal/walnut-frames/AllTogether.webp" alt="All three frames" />
        <img src="/images/journal/walnut-frames/DeepCorner.webp" alt="Corner detail" />
      </div>

    </div>

    <footer>
      <p>Heartwood Stand<br />Work that starts in the forest.</p>
    </footer>

  </body>
</html>